From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:14:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Horizon on Linux: SVCs, IPC and sm:, nn::init::Start boot;
 trap words lift; svc wrappers are entries; peek/poke keep the run's jump
 buffer

horizon_hle.py implements the SVCs a retail SDK issues (memory, GetInfo, handles, waits, IPC framing) and the nn::init::Start order of host/main.c; horizon_services.py has sm: and lm. Found booting Xenoblade Chronicles 2: an undefined-encoding word (0xe7ffdefe) made 18 functions unliftable, exported svc wrappers sharing one unwind entry were not entries, and aot_peek/aot_poke reset the run's jump buffer to null.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: S7bis, the Linux Horizon layer (SVCs, IPC, sm:, boot order) plus three AOT fixes found booting Xenoblade 2; tests use synthetic code and a fake guest memory, no game data
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

